/-
Johnson/AtFull/Shape/RuleAtTable.lean: THE TABLE OF STEPS ON SHAPES OF THE PROOF FILE's OWN FIRST
CHAIN (Johnson/AtFull/Shape/TableBatch.lean: `table_all`), BROUGHT TO THE FORMS OF THE FILE's RULE
FOR ACCEPTANCE WITH THE THIRD FAMILY (`file_acceptsJ`,
Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/Thread/FileJ.lean [not in this library]; the rule is not
called): THE TWO DEBTS THAT THE RULE ASKS AT EVERY MEMBER OF THE FIRST CHAIN, IN THE RULE's OWN
FORMS, AND ITS DEBT AT THE START. Under the head `P5J.AtMgA`; general in the three public files (in
the goals' scope); a joining of laws; nothing is evaluated here.

WHAT IT IS WORTH, FIRST. THREE PREMISES STAY, BY NAME, AND THEY ARE THE WEIGHT: (1) the run on
shapes returns over all 358 members (`Shape.yes`): a closed question at given public files, ANSWERED
BY NO THEOREM; many steps have a guard on the shape in front, and the run stops where one refuses;
(2) `FitsAt` at every member: what the honest side plays and reads passes the member's own tests on
rounds and columns; (3) `Values` at every member: what it plays passes the member's named tests on
values: at the proximity test, the batchings, the tails and the reads' sendings these tests run the
member's own work once more. WHAT IS CALLED "VALUES" IS MORE THAN VALUES: at the 25 numbers 14 l +
11 (l < 24) and 349 the table's test is oneV, which asks (usedOf s).isSome and four tests on sizes
beside its tests on values (ValsBool.lean's head says so); at the 25 closings (14 l + 12, l < 24,
and 350) it is closeInOrdB (CloseInOrder.lean): whoever pays `Values` owes facts on structure there.
No law that this file reaches shows oneV to accept. closeInOrdB is shown to accept at every state
reached in front of a closing (closeInOrdB_reached, closeInOrdB_at_closing: CloseInOrder.lean), with
"reached" in that file's own form; these laws do not show that a state is reached there; by its
Limits no theorem of that file joins the accept to `Values`, and none here does. SOME CLAUSES OF THE
TABLE's TESTS ON VALUES HANG ON THE DRAWS (an element that is drawn, or made of draws, is not 0):
wherever the thread comes to an event at which such a clause fails (Thr holds, the draws fit,
nothing of the member stops, the prover's side has moved), `Values` wants a fall that speaks there,
and the rule then asks of the run that no fall spoke; that a thread comes to such an event is not
shown here. fall, T, Said AND a₀ ARE FREE LETTERS HERE: one equation ties T.bs = cF.blocksInOrder; beyond it
they stand under the three named premises alone (in first_chain_debts_halved under h4 and `ValuesJ`
in the stead of (2) and (3)). SO THE PREMISE ON THE VALUES AND BOTH CONCLUSIONS CAN HOLD EMPTILY: at
a fall that always speaks; AT EVERY fall, at a thread whose Thr never holds; `ValuesJ` and both
conclusions also at a Said that never holds, and at an a₀ whose run returns the shape of no state at
which the thread stands. AND THE RULE ITSELF ASKS MUCH MORE THAN THESE TWO DEBTS (below).

Main names.
* `carriesU_of_V`: `CarriesV` (Johnson/AtFull/Shape/BatchFrames.lean) is `CarriesU`
  (Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/Thread/ShapeJ.lean): one text under two names.
* `debts_of_both`: GENERAL, at any thread T, any shape and any n with T.bs.length = n: the run on
  shapes returns over n members; `CarriesU`, `Returns`, `FitsAt` and `Values` at every member below
  n: then `AcceptedJ` and `NextJ` at every member, at the family "the run on shapes over the members
  in front returns the state's shape" (`shapeJ`). By `acceptedJ_of_shape` and `nextJ_of_shape`,
  member by member.
* `shapeJ_start`: that family holds at border 0 at a state whose own shape the run starts from.
* `first_chain_debts`: UNDER THE HEAD, with Bs what `ProofFile.baseOf` returns at the public part, at the
  table's own letters, FOR EVERY THREAD T WITH T.bs = cF.blocksInOrder AND EVERY Said, fall AND a₀: under the
  three named premises: `AcceptedJ` and `NextJ` at every member: the premises y₁ and c₁ of
  `file_acceptsJ`. `CarriesU` and `Returns` are paid by `table_all`; the number 358 by `flat_len`
  (Johnson/AtFull/Shape/Numbers.lean).
* `debts_of_bothV`, `first_chain_debts_halved`: THE SAME TWO DEBTS FROM OTHER PREMISES. In
  first_chain_debts_halved, in the stead of `FitsAt` at every member (debts_of_bothV keeps it): one
  test with code, `halved cF.blocksInOrder T.hs` (Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/Law/Run.lean: at each member
  a prover's side is at its place, or none of its rounds declares an item other than a root), by
  `fitsAt_of_halved` (Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/Thread/FitsAll.lean): it gives FitsAt; no law
  here gives it from FitsAt. In the stead of `Values`: `ValuesJ`
  (Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/Thread/ShapeJV.lean): the same with the family in hand at the state
  in front, which `Values` gives (`valuesJ_of`). That the test passes at any prover is not shown.
* `startShA`, `start_shA`: under the head, at every instance whose request passes the tests that
  need no reply, the first state's whole shape (the chain's shape and the rows' makes) is one
  written value: so a₀ can be a closed term. Over `start_at`
  (Johnson/AtFull/Shape/StartAtHead.lean).
* `first_chain_start`: so the rule's premise j₁ holds at a₀ := `startShA`.

WHAT THE RULE ASKS BESIDES, none of it here: that the three threads sit on the file and the prover;
the file's tests on the plan and on the instance; that the prover's side is ready, the draws are as
many as are due, and no part stops; what each thread owes and says, member by member, at all draws,
and what is said at the two starts; the two entries; the door behind the first two chains, and that
it returns; the family at the second chain's start and across the door; the file's last test; that
the run returned, and that no fall speaks along it; the like two debts for the other two chains. The
rule ends in `FileDescription.run`'s yes, not in a verifier's accept.

Limits. As above. IN WHAT THIS FILE REACHES NO STATE IS SHOWN AT WHICH A STEP RETURNS, A GUARD
ACCEPTS OR A TEST ACCEPTS: closeInOrdB's law (above) speaks at every state reached in front of a
closing and shows none to be reached. The like laws on switchW and linkGd stand in files that this
one does not reach (TableBatch.lean's Limits name them). The one road to premise (1) that is laid
(YesAtZFullN.lean; JoinTable.lean) has the head at VerifierAndGoals.storedPublicFiles, stands under hsz, and has the
closed line, or all pieces of the run, as a premise; for VerifierAndGoals.zGap none is laid. That the head has
a member is shown at named sets of public files alone, in a side library. At the format's second
hash function. Nothing on soundness, completeness or hiding.
-/
import Johnson.AtFull.Shape.TableBatch
import Johnson.AtFull.Shape.StartAtHead
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.Thread.ShapeJV
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.Thread.FitsAll

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

namespace Johnson.AtFull.Shape
open OnBytes OnBytes.Model
open VerifiableInference.Desc (Block Chain)
open VerifiableInference.Desc.First (S)
open VerifiableInference.Desc.First.Shape
open OnBytes.Maker (WholeD)
open P5J (AtMgA)
open ProofFile.Honest (Shape Thread Coins Mid ProverCoinCounts Returns FitsAt Values CarriesU NextJ AcceptedJ shapeJ
  nextJ_of_shape acceptedJ_of_shape ValuesJ nextJ_of_shapeV acceptedJ_of_shapeV halved
  fitsAt_of_halved)

/-! ## 1 General -/

/-- One text under two names. -/
theorem carriesU_of_V {Cl : Type} {bs : List (Block S Cl)} {ft : Nat} {Zs : Shape S} {b : Nat}
    (h : CarriesV bs ft Zs b) : CarriesU bs ft Zs b := h

/-- **GENERAL: the two debts at every member, from the cut's four forms at every member.** -/
theorem debts_of_both {σ Cl V W X Pb : Type} {Bk : ProverCoinCounts} (T : Thread Bk σ Cl V W X Pb)
    (Said : Nat → Coins Bk → Mid W X → Prop) (Zs : Shape σ) {a₀ : Zs.Sh} {n : Nat}
    {fall : Nat → σ → List Fmt.Drawn → Option String} (hn : T.bs.length = n)
    (hyes : Zs.yes a₀ n = true) (hC : ∀ b, b < n → CarriesU T.bs T.ft Zs b)
    (hR : ∀ b, b < n → Returns T.bs T.ft Zs b) (hF : ∀ b, b < n → FitsAt T b)
    (hV : ∀ b, b < n → Values T Zs fall b) :
    (∀ b, b < T.bs.length → AcceptedJ T Said (shapeJ Zs a₀) fall b) ∧
      (∀ b, b < T.bs.length → NextJ T Said (shapeJ Zs a₀) fall b) := by
  subst hn
  exact ⟨fun b hb => acceptedJ_of_shape T Said Zs hb hyes (hR b hb) (hF b hb) (hV b hb),
    fun b hb => nextJ_of_shape T Said Zs hb hyes (hC b hb) (hV b hb)⟩

/-- **GENERAL: the same from less**: the values are asked with the family in hand. -/
theorem debts_of_bothV {σ Cl V W X Pb : Type} {Bk : ProverCoinCounts} (T : Thread Bk σ Cl V W X Pb)
    (Said : Nat → Coins Bk → Mid W X → Prop) (Zs : Shape σ) {a₀ : Zs.Sh} {n : Nat}
    {fall : Nat → σ → List Fmt.Drawn → Option String} (hn : T.bs.length = n)
    (hyes : Zs.yes a₀ n = true) (hC : ∀ b, b < n → CarriesU T.bs T.ft Zs b)
    (hR : ∀ b, b < n → Returns T.bs T.ft Zs b) (hF : ∀ b, b < n → FitsAt T b)
    (hV : ∀ b, b < n → ValuesJ T Said (shapeJ Zs a₀) Zs fall b) :
    (∀ b, b < T.bs.length → AcceptedJ T Said (shapeJ Zs a₀) fall b) ∧
      (∀ b, b < T.bs.length → NextJ T Said (shapeJ Zs a₀) fall b) := by
  subst hn
  exact ⟨fun b hb => acceptedJ_of_shapeV T Said Zs hb hyes (hR b hb) (hF b hb) (hV b hb),
    fun b hb => nextJ_of_shapeV T Said Zs hb hyes (hC b hb) (hV b hb)⟩

/-- The family holds at border 0 at a state from whose own shape the run starts. -/
theorem shapeJ_start {σ : Type} (Zs : Shape σ) (s₀ : σ) : shapeJ Zs (Zs.sh s₀) 0 s₀ := rfl

/-! ## 2 Under the head, at the table -/

variable {Z : VerifierAndGoals.PublicFiles} {D : WholeD} {r : LPFD.Full.RunPF} {Zp : ProofFile.Pub} {Np : H2U.Places4}
  {cF : Chain S ProofFile.Cl} {x : VerifiableInference.Desc.First.Look.Place} {Bs : ProofFile.PureBase}

/-- **THE FIRST CHAIN's TWO DEBTS IN THE FILE's RULE, AT THE TABLE**: under the run on shapes, the
fits and the values. -/
theorem first_chain_debts (h : AtMgA OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D r Zp Np cF x)
    (hB : ProofFile.baseOf Zp (ProofFile.pureSeat OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp) = .ok Bs) {V W X Pb : Type} {Bk : ProverCoinCounts}
    (T : Thread Bk S ProofFile.Cl V W X Pb) (hbs : T.bs = cF.blocksInOrder)
    (Said : Nat → Coins Bk → Mid W X → Prop)
    (fall : Nat → S → List Fmt.Drawn → Option String) (a₀ : ShA)
    (hyes : (firstZA (Tab.g Zp Bs.G₀) (Tab.vals Zp Bs.G₀)).yes a₀ 358 = true)
    (hF : ∀ b, b < 358 → FitsAt T b)
    (hV : ∀ b, b < 358 → Values T (firstZA (Tab.g Zp Bs.G₀) (Tab.vals Zp Bs.G₀)) fall b) :
    (∀ b, b < T.bs.length →
        AcceptedJ T Said (shapeJ (firstZA (Tab.g Zp Bs.G₀) (Tab.vals Zp Bs.G₀)) a₀) fall b) ∧
      (∀ b, b < T.bs.length →
        NextJ T Said (shapeJ (firstZA (Tab.g Zp Bs.G₀) (Tab.vals Zp Bs.G₀)) a₀) fall b) :=
  debts_of_both T Said _ (by rw [hbs]; exact flat_len h) hyes
    (fun b hb => by rw [hbs]; exact carriesU_of_V (table_all h hB b hb T.ft).1)
    (fun b hb => by rw [hbs]; exact (table_all h hB b hb T.ft).2) hF hV

/-- **THE SAME TWO DEBTS FROM OTHER PREMISES**: one test with code on the chain's list and the
prover's sides in the stead of the fits (it gives them; no law here gives it from them); the values
asked with the family in hand (the weaker premise). -/
theorem first_chain_debts_halved (h : AtMgA OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D r Zp Np cF x)
    (hB : ProofFile.baseOf Zp (ProofFile.pureSeat OnBytes.secondHashFunction Zp) = .ok Bs) {V W X Pb : Type} {Bk : ProverCoinCounts}
    (T : Thread Bk S ProofFile.Cl V W X Pb) (hbs : T.bs = cF.blocksInOrder)
    (Said : Nat → Coins Bk → Mid W X → Prop)
    (fall : Nat → S → List Fmt.Drawn → Option String) (a₀ : ShA)
    (hyes : (firstZA (Tab.g Zp Bs.G₀) (Tab.vals Zp Bs.G₀)).yes a₀ 358 = true)
    (h4 : halved cF.blocksInOrder T.hs = true)
    (hV : ∀ b, b < 358 →
      ValuesJ T Said (shapeJ (firstZA (Tab.g Zp Bs.G₀) (Tab.vals Zp Bs.G₀)) a₀)
        (firstZA (Tab.g Zp Bs.G₀) (Tab.vals Zp Bs.G₀)) fall b) :
    (∀ b, b < T.bs.length →
        AcceptedJ T Said (shapeJ (firstZA (Tab.g Zp Bs.G₀) (Tab.vals Zp Bs.G₀)) a₀) fall b) ∧
      (∀ b, b < T.bs.length →
        NextJ T Said (shapeJ (firstZA (Tab.g Zp Bs.G₀) (Tab.vals Zp Bs.G₀)) a₀) fall b) :=
  debts_of_bothV T Said _ (by rw [hbs]; exact flat_len h) hyes
    (fun b hb => by rw [hbs]; exact carriesU_of_V (table_all h hB b hb T.ft).1)
    (fun b hb => by rw [hbs]; exact (table_all h hB b hb T.ft).2)
    (fun b _ => fitsAt_of_halved T (by rw [hbs]; exact h4) b) hV

/-- The first state's whole shape at the full size: a closed term. -/
def startShA : ShA := (startShFull, formsOf startFull.st)

/-- **Under the head, where the request passes, the first state's whole shape is the written
one.** -/
theorem start_shA (h : AtMgA OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D r Zp Np cF x) (p : ProofFile.InstPub)
    (hp : (Zp.s₀.withReq (Verify.words32 p.request)).reqOk Zp.p.X.T Zp.p.X.P.h.V = true) :
    shA (ProofFile.startS Zp p) = startShA := by
  have e : (ProofFile.startS Zp p).st = startFull.st := by
    unfold ProofFile.startS
    simp only [hp, if_true]
    show Zp.s₀.st = _
    rw [s₀_at h]
  unfold shA chainF startShA
  rw [start_at h p hp, e]

/-- **The rule's debt at the first chain's start**, at the written shape. -/
theorem first_chain_start (h : AtMgA OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D r Zp Np cF x) (p : ProofFile.InstPub)
    (hp : (Zp.s₀.withReq (Verify.words32 p.request)).reqOk Zp.p.X.T Zp.p.X.P.h.V = true)
    (g : Nat → ShA → Except String ShA)
    (vals : Nat → S → List Fmt.RoundView → List (List (Nat × List UInt64)) → Bool) :
    shapeJ (firstZA g vals) startShA 0 (ProofFile.startS Zp p) := by
  have e := shapeJ_start (firstZA g vals) (ProofFile.startS Zp p)
  have e' : (firstZA g vals).sh (ProofFile.startS Zp p) = startShA := start_shA h p hp
  rw [e'] at e
  exact e

end Johnson.AtFull.Shape

